cue0140044
00:55:17.488 --> 00:55:24.488
That is one of the great contributions of the Shulḥan ʿArukh is precisely in omitting anything to do with capital punishment.

cue0140045
00:55:24.488 --> 00:55:32.488
The Tumul of the Shukran is the capital punishment. And therefore, because he says very clearly that capital punishment is no longer to be practiced among Jews.

cue0140046
00:55:32.488 --> 00:55:43.488
So therefore, all the problems involved with laws which by the time that the Shukran Haruch was composed were no longer part of the civilized horizon,

cue0140047
00:55:43.488 --> 00:55:56.688
The Shukharuch very intelligently, he solves the problem by saying capital cases no longer tried by Jews.

cue0140048
00:55:56.688 --> 00:56:04.088
And by omitting, and in a way the Shukharuch becomes stronger and stronger.

cue0140049
00:56:04.088 --> 00:56:13.088
And this is the answer to your question. All those laws are just omitted by the Shukharuch, not brought into...

cue0140050
00:56:13.088 --> 00:56:20.328
